course: dictionary
lesson: 7051
title: One word, many meanings: past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word past has more than one meaning, so you must read the words around it to find the right one. Ask yourself: is this about time, about moving by something, or about going beyond a place?
explain: «Half past three» is 3:30. Here past means after the hour. «She ran past the gate» is different: past means going by the gate. Both use the same word, but the clues are different.
explain: «Learning about the past helps us understand today.» Here the past is time that has gone, before now. As an adjective, past can mean just gone, as in «the past week».
fact: Past can be a noun, an adjective, a preposition or an adverb.
fact: The past is time that has gone, before now.
fact: As a preposition, past means going by something, as in «he walked past the shop».
fact: In telling time, past means after the hour: «10 past 4» is 4:10.
fact: Past also means beyond, as in «past midnight» or «past the bridge». Read the clues to decide which meaning is right.
exercise: In «Half past three», what time is it? | 3:03 | 4:30 | *3:30 | 3:15
exercise: «The Year 3s hid behind the climbing frame whenever Jake walked past.» What does past mean here? | Before now | *Went by | Beyond the end of the school day | Just finished
exercise: «Learning about the past helps us understand today.» What is the past here? | A day after tomorrow | The front of a line | A type of bridge | *Time that has gone, before now
test: «Past midnight, the house was quiet.» What does past mean here? | *Beyond midnight, after it | Going by the house | Just finished | Before midnight
test: In «the past 3 days», what does past mean? | Going by three days | Three days long in the story | Days far in the future | *Just gone, the last three days
exam: Which use of past means just gone, as in «the past week»? | She ran past the gate | Half past three is the time | *The past week was wet and cold | Learning about the past is fun
